<ReferenceLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="RadMage Finance works without collecting information about you: no accounts, no cookies, no analytics, and calculations that stay on your device."
  lead="RadMage Finance is built to work without collecting information about you."
  updated="2026-11-16"
>
  <h2>What is stored on your device</h2>
  <p>
    One setting: your theme choice (Dark, Light or System). It is saved in your browser's
    local storage under the name <code>rmf-theme</code>, so the site looks the way you chose on
    your next visit. It never leaves your device, and clearing this site's data in your browser
    removes it.
  </p>

  <h2>What is not collected</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No accounts and no sign-up.</li>
    <li>No cookies.</li>
    <li>No analytics, advertising or tracking scripts.</li>
    <li>No third-party fonts, scripts, embeds or other requests to outside services.</li>
    <li>Nothing you type into a calculator or lesson. All calculations run in your browser.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Share links</h2>
  <p>
    Where a calculator offers a share link, the scenario is stored in the link itself, after
    the <code>#</code> sign. Browsers do not send that part of an address to any server, so
    the numbers never reach this site, and nothing is saved here.
  </p>
  <p>That keeps the numbers off the servers that deliver this site, but it does not make the link private:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Anyone who has the link can read everything in it, amounts included.</li>
    <li>The whole link stays wherever it goes: in your browser history and on any device that syncs it, in the message, email or document you paste it into, and with the app or service that delivers it.</li>
    <li>Browser extensions you have installed can read the addresses of the pages you visit, including this part.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Before you copy a link you can choose how dollar amounts go into it: exactly, rounded to
    their first two digits, or not at all. Rounded amounts are still close to your own; with
    No amounts the link keeps only the rates, the years and the other choices.
  </p>

  <h2>Reports, CSV files and printing</h2>
  <p>
    A calculator's report, CSV file and text summary are made in your browser and saved
    straight to your device; nothing is uploaded. Their file names hold only the calculator,
    the kind of file and the date, never an amount you entered. The report is a single
    file that loads nothing from the internet. Once saved, a file is like any other document:
    anyone you send it to can read your figures.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
  <p>
    Two services deliver these pages. The RadMage Labs website, radmagelabs.com, runs on
    Vercel, which receives each request and fetches the Finance pages from GitHub Pages,
    where they are published. Vercel passes your IP address on to GitHub with each request.
    The same pages are also published at radmageirl.github.io/finance/, where only GitHub
    handles the request.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Vercel says it collects "information about traffic to and from Customers' websites, such as End User IP address, location information derived from IP address, and system configuration information." (<a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-notice">Vercel Privacy Notice</a>, effective June 1, 2026; on passing the visitor's address to the origin, <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/routing/rewrites">Vercel's rewrites documentation</a>)</li>
    <li>GitHub says that "when a GitHub Pages site is visited, the visitor's IP address is logged and stored for security purposes, regardless of whether the visitor has signed into GitHub or not." (<a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages">What is GitHub Pages?</a>; <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>, effective April 27, 2026)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Those records belong to the hosting services and follow their own policies. RadMage
    Finance adds no tracking of its own, and none of what you type into a calculator or
    lesson is sent to either service. Hosting details checked November 16, 2026.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If anything here changes, for example if advertising is ever added, this page will be
    updated first and the change dated.
  </p>
</ReferenceLayout>
